WEBVTT

00:50.341 --> 00:52.260
Dating is like

00:52.927 --> 00:54.679
living in a different world.

00:56.389 --> 00:58.141
Dating Yeon-su

00:58.933 --> 01:00.477
is especially

01:01.478 --> 01:03.313
a completely different world for me.

01:06.024 --> 01:08.026
Ung!

01:08.109 --> 01:08.943
What?

01:09.736 --> 01:10.820
What is it?

01:12.280 --> 01:13.239
What's going on?

01:17.494 --> 01:19.245
- Why did you call me?
- It's bedtime.

01:19.329 --> 01:20.413
What?

01:21.331 --> 01:23.541
It's only 10 p.m. I can't sleep now.

01:26.961 --> 01:29.964
I drank all the jujube tea.
Where did you get this?

01:30.632 --> 01:33.468
- Is there a well of it in my house?
- Drink up and go to bed.

01:34.052 --> 01:37.680
I can't sleep at this hour.
Even kids don't sleep this early.

01:37.764 --> 01:39.766
Should I sleep over too?

01:47.899 --> 01:49.567
We should sleep since it's dark.

01:49.651 --> 01:52.278
It's dangerous
to be out and about at this hour.

01:55.281 --> 01:56.449
Let's go to bed.

01:59.702 --> 02:00.578
No!

02:00.662 --> 02:02.163
- Wake up!
- Jeez.

02:02.247 --> 02:04.791
Do you want me to sleep or not?
Make a choice.

02:04.874 --> 02:07.460
You can't sleep at night
because you sleep in the morning.

02:07.544 --> 02:10.338
You have to endure this
to get back a normal sleep cycle.

02:10.421 --> 02:11.464
Run!

02:13.424 --> 02:14.801
But as you know,

02:15.301 --> 02:18.012
that world doesn't really suit me.

02:19.347 --> 02:21.141
What can I do though?

02:21.224 --> 02:23.268
The bus is here. See you.

02:23.351 --> 02:24.727
Wait, Yeon-su!

02:28.606 --> 02:29.691
Bye!

02:29.774 --> 02:31.234
- Yeon-su.
- Yes?

02:33.069 --> 02:34.154
Bye.

02:47.667 --> 02:48.543
What are you doing?

02:49.252 --> 02:51.379
I just came home after work.

02:51.462 --> 02:53.673
You got off work late.
Did you have dinner?

02:53.756 --> 02:57.051
Yes, I ate at the place you recommended
and it was really good.

02:57.135 --> 02:59.137
- Let's go there next time.
- Okay.

02:59.220 --> 03:01.931
Back then and even now…

03:09.981 --> 03:11.858
I want to keep living in this world.

03:14.444 --> 03:15.612
Forever,

03:16.487 --> 03:17.572
without an end.

03:19.073 --> 03:19.991
Let's break up.

03:20.074 --> 03:21.743
You're the only thing

03:22.577 --> 03:23.953
I can throw away.

03:24.037 --> 03:25.538
Why are you doing this?

03:26.164 --> 03:28.333
Why do we have to break up?

03:36.591 --> 03:38.051
Those are useless thoughts.

03:40.929 --> 03:43.014
LIKE WATER FOR CHOCOLATE

03:45.516 --> 03:47.435
I have to be more cautious
at a time like this.

03:47.518 --> 03:48.603
THE LIKELIHOOD OF STAYING IN
A RELATIONSHIP WITH YOUR EX

03:48.686 --> 03:51.564
Because misfortune always comes
disguised as happiness.

03:54.901 --> 03:58.905
"Couples who fight often have
a higher chance of dating again."

04:01.241 --> 04:06.120
"But they think they will
still be the same after they do

04:06.788 --> 04:09.123
and have lower expectations
of each other."

04:09.999 --> 04:12.043
"To maintain your relationship,

04:12.627 --> 04:16.130
you must show your partner
a new side of you

04:16.714 --> 04:20.677
to break such expectations."

04:23.221 --> 04:26.516
I shouldn't lower my guard because
it seems like everything's going okay.

04:27.850 --> 04:31.646
So I believe I need to prepare myself
for possible risks.

04:33.022 --> 04:34.482
"A new side…"

04:34.565 --> 04:36.484
I went through so much to get here.

04:38.945 --> 04:41.114
I can't repeat the same mistakes.

04:55.795 --> 05:00.967
EPISODE 13

05:07.765 --> 05:09.600
I want to stay with you.

05:10.935 --> 05:11.811
Come here.

05:23.364 --> 05:24.574
What do we do about him?

05:25.616 --> 05:27.368
I'll take care of it. Go to work.

05:27.869 --> 05:28.703
What will you do?

05:29.329 --> 05:30.872
Is there a brick anywhere?

05:31.748 --> 05:33.916
Take care of this quietly
so there's no fuss.

05:35.001 --> 05:36.252
- Bye.
- Bye.

05:44.844 --> 05:46.804
What…

05:48.890 --> 05:52.185
Hey, inhale through your nose
and exhale through your mouth.

05:56.689 --> 05:57.523
That's right.

05:59.692 --> 06:01.486
What was that?

06:02.361 --> 06:03.196
It just happened.

06:03.863 --> 06:04.739
"It just happened"?

06:05.239 --> 06:06.365
Don't overreact.

06:07.617 --> 06:10.620
Wait, since when? How long has it been?

06:11.829 --> 06:13.998
So you didn't let me come
to your house because…

06:14.791 --> 06:17.043
No, forget all that.

06:17.126 --> 06:19.420
Who knows about this? Does Ji-ung know?

06:21.672 --> 06:23.007
Then what about Sol-i?

06:24.133 --> 06:25.134
She probably knows.

06:26.719 --> 06:30.056
- What about your parents?
- They know.

06:30.890 --> 06:33.476
- But is that important?
- I'm so disappointed.

06:34.310 --> 06:37.355
I'm very disappointed.
How could you not tell only me?

06:38.189 --> 06:39.023
How could you?

06:39.607 --> 06:41.818
- Are you crying?
- How could you do this to me?

06:41.901 --> 06:45.238
- No way!
- Is he crazy? Wait, Eun-ho!

06:47.031 --> 06:48.366
Good morning.

06:48.449 --> 06:49.909
- Hi, Ms. Kook.
- Good morning.

06:57.333 --> 07:00.711
Failed to deal with Eun-ho.
I'll wait for my next chance.

07:09.345 --> 07:10.513
Oh, Mr. Bang.

07:11.222 --> 07:13.099
Do you have good news?

07:13.599 --> 07:15.393
No, nothing.

07:16.060 --> 07:17.728
It seems like there is.

07:18.896 --> 07:20.690
Why are you whispering though?

07:22.400 --> 07:24.902
There's a terrible rumor
going around these days.

07:26.904 --> 07:28.156
What rumor?

07:28.656 --> 07:31.325
That you're dating someone.

07:38.291 --> 07:39.125
Says who?

07:42.044 --> 07:43.921
It's all right. Don't get worked up.

07:45.131 --> 07:48.426
This rumor is so terrible
that I told everyone it wasn't true.

07:48.509 --> 07:50.136
"Ms. Kook would never do that."

07:50.219 --> 07:53.431
"She doesn't have any love for humanity."

07:53.514 --> 07:55.391
"She's not human." I told everyone that.

07:57.268 --> 07:58.811
That's not why I'm here though.

07:59.479 --> 08:02.732
I got a call from Soen
about the documentary you were shooting.

08:02.815 --> 08:06.068
They asked if they could see
the footage you have before it airs.

08:06.152 --> 08:08.029
And I'm curious too.

08:08.112 --> 08:12.074
- We must be in quite a lot, right?
- All right. I'll ask.

08:12.158 --> 08:14.744
When does it start airing again?
Isn't it soon?

08:15.786 --> 08:19.123
Oh, and I was interviewed for it.

08:19.207 --> 08:21.167
Tell them never to edit it out

08:21.792 --> 08:23.920
and just air it as is, okay?

08:25.963 --> 08:26.797
Cool.

08:39.769 --> 08:41.020
KIM JI-UNG

08:44.941 --> 08:47.568
The person you have called cannot…

08:50.112 --> 08:54.075
HOW IS EDITING GOING?

08:57.078 --> 08:58.371
I guess he's busy.

09:02.333 --> 09:04.794
I've never seen him like that before.

09:04.877 --> 09:05.878
It feels as if

09:06.504 --> 09:07.630
he has changed.

09:07.713 --> 09:09.507
I thought he'd never change.

09:10.633 --> 09:12.426
END OF FIRST DRAFT
PREVIEW TO BE ADDED

09:17.848 --> 09:18.724
Mr. Kim.

09:20.893 --> 09:22.645
You've found your direction.

09:24.939 --> 09:26.983
This is great for a first draft.

09:28.568 --> 09:31.404
I knew you'd do well.

09:31.487 --> 09:33.864
I'll fix the last narration part.
I don't like it.

09:33.948 --> 09:35.032
All right.

09:35.116 --> 09:39.203
But they haven't changed at all.
They still seem so young and lively.

09:39.287 --> 09:42.999
There's some tension between them too.
I'm curious about the next episode.

09:43.082 --> 09:44.834
I'm really satisfied with this.

09:45.418 --> 09:46.252
That's a relief.

09:47.336 --> 09:48.963
Stop asking to see it now.

09:49.046 --> 09:50.172
Fine.

09:50.256 --> 09:53.634
Is it normal for the team leader
to beg his team member to see his work?

09:53.718 --> 09:55.219
Do you think that's normal?

09:57.054 --> 09:58.014
It's ridiculous.

09:58.097 --> 10:00.141
All right, what are you
all doing after work?

10:00.224 --> 10:03.185
We should celebrate
since the first draft is finished.

10:03.269 --> 10:04.520
I have to work.

10:05.104 --> 10:07.773
What's so urgent? Let's go have some fun!

10:07.857 --> 10:10.192
Should a team leader be
saying that? I'm off.

10:19.410 --> 10:20.244
Is he okay?

10:21.078 --> 10:22.413
What?

10:23.122 --> 10:24.290
Did you see his eyes?

10:25.333 --> 10:26.959
He seems to have lost his mind.

10:29.253 --> 10:31.714
Make sure he eats his meals properly.

10:31.797 --> 10:34.800
You should eat well
when you're in pain inside.

10:34.884 --> 10:37.386
I'll make sure he eats well.

10:37.970 --> 10:42.016
Hey, you should take care of me.
I feel lonely these days.

10:42.099 --> 10:43.976
It's as if I'm a ghost
haunting this place.

10:44.060 --> 10:47.647
And what do you mean?
He looks absolutely fine.

10:47.730 --> 10:49.732
He's not the only one who's busy.
We all are!

10:50.232 --> 10:51.192
EDITING ROOM

11:18.928 --> 11:22.181
What's the new special documentary about?

11:22.264 --> 11:24.642
Next year is
the tenth anniversary of my debut.

11:24.725 --> 11:28.646
So I'm preparing
a special video for my fans.

11:28.729 --> 11:30.815
So it's been ten years already.

11:30.898 --> 11:34.151
You must feel so many emotions right now.

11:35.111 --> 11:36.862
Yes, I do.

11:37.822 --> 11:39.698
It gave me a lot to think about.

11:39.782 --> 11:45.037
Lastly, I believe many people
are curious about this--

11:45.121 --> 11:46.080
The scandal?

11:47.415 --> 11:49.083
This may be a sensitive topic,

11:49.166 --> 11:52.795
but could you reveal anything about that
to the viewers of Litte

11:52.878 --> 11:54.964
who are watching this show live right now?

11:55.548 --> 11:57.508
Sure. Why not?

11:58.676 --> 12:01.762
Are you really dating him right now?

12:02.430 --> 12:04.849
No, we're not dating.

12:06.308 --> 12:07.435
But I like him.

12:09.061 --> 12:11.897
- Pardon?
- Of course, as a fan.

12:13.441 --> 12:15.901
At first, he said that he was my fan.

12:16.527 --> 12:18.154
But now I'm a fan of his.

12:18.737 --> 12:20.489
So I wanted to become his friend,

12:21.323 --> 12:24.493
but I feel like we've grown distant
since the article was released.

12:26.495 --> 12:30.291
So everyone, please don't make
wild speculations about us.

12:30.374 --> 12:31.792
Please.

12:33.085 --> 12:35.212
NJ is just a victim in all this.

12:35.796 --> 12:37.256
It's because of that traitor.

12:37.339 --> 12:38.966
Just pick a side, will you?

12:39.049 --> 12:42.136
If you're going to be angry at me,
do it at home. Why are you here?

12:42.761 --> 12:46.265
I have to work, so I'm putting up
with breathing the same air as you.

12:46.932 --> 12:49.810
How are the preparations
for your exhibition going?

12:50.394 --> 12:52.813
I got a lot done.
Have you ever see me behind schedule?

12:55.774 --> 12:57.860
But where are you even looking?

12:59.153 --> 13:00.821
- Who knows?
- What?

13:00.905 --> 13:03.782
You could neglect your drawings
since you're dating now.

13:04.450 --> 13:07.036
- Stop that.
- Can you even focus on work?

13:07.119 --> 13:09.872
You neglect everything when you're dating.

13:09.955 --> 13:11.540
- Eun-ho, are you--
- I just don't get why

13:11.624 --> 13:14.460
you're seeing Yeon-su again.

13:14.543 --> 13:15.377
What?

13:15.461 --> 13:18.130
You were in so much pain.
Do you want to go through it again?

13:18.214 --> 13:21.008
Did you forget how many times
you've been through this?

13:21.091 --> 13:23.886
Should I remind you
how bad things got each time?

13:24.470 --> 13:26.514
I don't want to see you
go through that again.

13:36.607 --> 13:37.441
What?

13:38.526 --> 13:39.527
What do you want?

13:45.449 --> 13:46.450
Come on.

13:47.076 --> 13:50.788
It wasn't that bad.
It's fine. I'll take care of myself.

13:51.747 --> 13:54.542
You were just going to do whatever
without telling me.

13:54.625 --> 13:56.001
I'm sorry about that.

13:56.752 --> 13:58.462
But I…

14:01.090 --> 14:03.175
I'm just in such a good mood these days.

14:04.552 --> 14:06.679
I'm so happy right now.
What else can I do?

14:11.100 --> 14:12.977
You disgust me.

14:14.728 --> 14:16.897
Anyway, it's different this time.

14:16.981 --> 14:18.607
I won't be like that again, okay?

14:25.406 --> 14:26.782
I'm hungry.

14:27.491 --> 14:28.701
Should we eat?

14:31.620 --> 14:33.205
Do you want to talk about work?

14:36.041 --> 14:40.170
Should we talk about that raise
you mentioned last time?

14:44.592 --> 14:45.676
Raise?

14:53.225 --> 14:56.520
Anyway, I'm going to be watching
the two of you.

14:59.481 --> 15:01.609
- I want a 30 percent raise.
- What?

15:03.444 --> 15:05.154
Then 25 percent.

15:09.575 --> 15:10.409
Twenty.

15:30.179 --> 15:31.513
Did you eat?

15:31.597 --> 15:34.558
Yes. You should eat too.

15:37.603 --> 15:38.604
UNG

15:38.687 --> 15:40.064
- What are you doing?
- I'm in a meeting.

15:40.147 --> 15:41.649
- I was about to eat.
- Okay.

15:41.732 --> 15:42.650
Did you finish work?

15:42.733 --> 15:44.276
Not yet. Leaving soon.

15:44.360 --> 15:45.277
YES, OKAY, NOT TODAY

15:46.362 --> 15:48.656
Were my replies too short?

15:48.739 --> 15:50.908
YOUR NEW SIDE

15:51.492 --> 15:55.204
I need to talk to more people
to find this new side of mine.

15:55.871 --> 15:58.248
Dating? It's no big deal.

15:58.332 --> 16:00.751
If a man and a woman like each other,
they date,

16:00.834 --> 16:03.253
and then they kiss,

16:03.337 --> 16:04.505
and then…

16:10.636 --> 16:11.470
Make eye contact,

16:11.553 --> 16:12.930
and say, "I love you."

16:14.056 --> 16:16.475
No, that's not a good example.

16:18.852 --> 16:21.105
Did you enjoy your lunch, Ms. Kook?

16:21.188 --> 16:22.731
Oh, yes.

16:31.657 --> 16:32.908
Ye-in.

16:32.992 --> 16:33.993
Yes?

16:34.576 --> 16:36.704
- Do you have a boyfriend?
- Me?

16:37.871 --> 16:41.166
No, why? Is there someone
you want to introduce to me?

16:41.959 --> 16:44.294
Then have you dated before?

16:44.962 --> 16:47.631
Of course I have.

16:47.715 --> 16:49.049
A lot.

16:50.509 --> 16:51.593
Then…

16:52.094 --> 16:56.181
were you good at dating?

16:58.434 --> 17:01.520
It might seem weird to say so myself,

17:01.603 --> 17:04.398
but if the company evaluated me
for my past relationships,

17:04.481 --> 17:08.193
I'd be the CEO here.

17:08.777 --> 17:10.946
- I see.
- But what's this about?

17:12.740 --> 17:13.741
Well…

17:16.160 --> 17:20.748
How exactly do you date?

17:24.918 --> 17:27.296
You've come to the perfect person.

17:45.439 --> 17:48.692
I'm getting off work soon.
Should we go on a date?

17:49.318 --> 17:51.695
Okay. I'll pick you up. wait there.

18:24.061 --> 18:24.895
Hi.

18:28.565 --> 18:29.858
Oh, hi.

18:30.609 --> 18:32.778
Your clothes have changed from earlier.

18:33.445 --> 18:37.116
Oh, I accidentally spilled something
so I bought a new outfit.

18:37.699 --> 18:39.952
You must have spilled a lot.

18:40.828 --> 18:42.287
- Let's go.
- Okay.

18:53.549 --> 18:57.094
First, visual stimulation
is very important.

18:57.177 --> 18:59.680
You have to style yourself
differently every now and then

18:59.763 --> 19:03.559
to create a tension
that isn't usually there.

19:18.365 --> 19:22.786
It would have been more effective
to just hit Eun-ho with a brick.

19:22.870 --> 19:25.247
It was so hard dealing with his sulking.

19:26.123 --> 19:29.084
And this is very, very important.

19:29.168 --> 19:33.505
Your reaction. Guys are crazy about
people who give great reactions.

19:33.589 --> 19:36.258
I was able to date so many guys
just with my reactions.

19:36.341 --> 19:38.844
React to whatever he does.
And smile a lot.

19:38.927 --> 19:41.930
What reason does he have to sulk?

19:42.014 --> 19:44.141
Sometimes he's so weird.

19:44.224 --> 19:45.976
- He must like me so much--
- Oh!

19:46.518 --> 19:49.146
- Really?
- What? Yes.

19:51.148 --> 19:52.191
It's so funny.

19:52.691 --> 19:53.859
What is?

19:55.485 --> 19:56.612
What?

19:56.695 --> 19:58.238
- What?
- What?

20:00.699 --> 20:02.993
And compliment him
as many times as you can.

20:03.911 --> 20:06.330
Hey, you're a really good driver…

20:07.372 --> 20:08.498
Sorry about that.

20:09.833 --> 20:11.418
What did you say? I missed that.

20:11.501 --> 20:12.753
It's nothing.

20:15.714 --> 20:19.176
They love being complimented,
even for the smallest things.

20:20.344 --> 20:22.721
You have really large hands.

20:22.804 --> 20:24.306
What? That's so random.

20:24.389 --> 20:26.183
They're so big.

20:26.767 --> 20:28.101
They're huge.

20:28.894 --> 20:29.770
I see.

20:31.688 --> 20:32.856
Right.

20:49.164 --> 20:50.499
Are you sure about this?

20:50.582 --> 20:51.917
You like Korean food better.

20:52.960 --> 20:55.921
Well, sometimes I crave food like this.

20:57.381 --> 21:00.634
I begged you for a month to go eat pasta
when we were in university.

21:00.717 --> 21:03.387
- We never did in the end.
- Did I do that?

21:04.638 --> 21:06.890
Well, people's tastes change.

21:07.808 --> 21:08.642
Oh, right.

21:09.935 --> 21:12.562
- Let me cut this for you.
- No, I'll do it. It's closer to me.

21:12.646 --> 21:14.106
Let me do it.

21:22.364 --> 21:25.617
And never nag him, Ms. Kook!

21:26.201 --> 21:28.954
Men despise nagging.

21:31.748 --> 21:32.916
I'm sorry.

21:33.000 --> 21:35.502
Excuse me, can I get a wet towel?

21:35.585 --> 21:38.672
No, it's fine. I'll wipe it off.

21:38.755 --> 21:43.468
I'm really sorry.
Are you sure it'll come off?

21:43.552 --> 21:45.345
It's fine. I'll get it dry cleaned.

21:45.429 --> 21:47.347
How did this happen?

21:47.431 --> 21:48.849
I told you I'd…

21:49.683 --> 21:52.561
I mean, I should have put this here.

21:53.770 --> 21:55.147
It was my bad.

22:00.027 --> 22:01.653
- Ung.
- Yes?

22:01.737 --> 22:04.323
- Eat up. Here.
- Okay.

22:06.116 --> 22:07.909
- Is it good?
- Yes.

22:27.804 --> 22:29.056
What are you thinking?

22:29.681 --> 22:33.351
It's been a long time since we walked
like this instead of running.

22:34.311 --> 22:35.145
What?

22:36.021 --> 22:40.275
We always ran because you thought
walking without a purpose

22:40.358 --> 22:42.527
was inefficient.

22:43.528 --> 22:45.739
- Did I do that?
- Yes.

22:46.531 --> 22:49.326
I bet we're the only ones
who ran around Deoksugung Palace.

22:50.786 --> 22:53.830
I guess I really was obsessed
with efficiency back then.

22:53.914 --> 22:55.373
I sound like a mess.

22:56.583 --> 22:58.293
You were cool though.

23:00.420 --> 23:02.047
And lastly…

23:02.130 --> 23:05.217
Keep making things romantic.

23:05.300 --> 23:07.010
Dating is all about

23:07.844 --> 23:09.304
having butterflies.

23:16.812 --> 23:19.940
This place is practically deserted.

23:21.191 --> 23:23.652
You're right.
It's not even that late though.

23:24.236 --> 23:26.530
How can this place be so empty?

23:31.660 --> 23:32.619
What…

23:45.090 --> 23:47.384
Why did you hit me?

23:48.927 --> 23:51.638
- What are you doing, Yeon-su?
- What do you mean?

23:51.721 --> 23:55.058
What has gotten into you today?
What's this character you're playing?

23:56.476 --> 23:58.520
You've been acting weird all day.

23:59.813 --> 24:00.856
What are you plotting?

24:01.648 --> 24:03.316
I'm not plotting anything.

24:03.400 --> 24:06.027
- I was making an effort.
- What effort?

24:06.945 --> 24:09.614
I'm trying to make
this relationship work out.

24:09.698 --> 24:10.657
What?

24:11.324 --> 24:13.743
Can't you see I'm trying to change

24:13.827 --> 24:15.829
so we'll stop fighting like before?

24:15.912 --> 24:18.081
Why do you have to do that?

24:18.165 --> 24:19.916
So that we don't break up.

24:20.542 --> 24:22.836
They say couples who fight
and break up often have

24:22.919 --> 24:24.671
a higher chance of breaking up again.

24:24.754 --> 24:27.799
And that they know each other so well
that they have no expectations.

24:28.925 --> 24:29.759
Who says?

24:30.343 --> 24:33.722
Dr. Yoo Yeong, human relationship
psychologist from Hankook University.

24:33.805 --> 24:35.473
That person doesn't know you.

24:36.266 --> 24:37.267
What?

24:37.350 --> 24:40.228
There are people like you
who are different each time.

24:42.314 --> 24:44.399
It feels new. Seeing you always feels new.

24:44.482 --> 24:46.610
It feels new even though
we met yesterday and again today.

24:48.653 --> 24:49.905
That's not what I mean.

24:49.988 --> 24:51.865
Look, you're different again.

24:51.948 --> 24:54.409
- You're different from three seconds ago.
- Stop.

24:55.368 --> 24:57.537
I've never thought
that you were predictable.

24:57.621 --> 25:00.624
If that was possible,
I would be the one with a Ph. D.

25:02.292 --> 25:04.044
But still,

25:04.127 --> 25:07.214
it felt like I was always nagging you

25:07.297 --> 25:10.258
and starting fights,

25:10.342 --> 25:11.927
so I was trying to stop that.

25:14.095 --> 25:16.640
I just like you for who you are.

25:18.225 --> 25:21.102
I like that you always have
new things to nag about.

25:23.730 --> 25:26.608
But I don't want you nagging
about the same thing twice.

25:27.651 --> 25:29.903
Always come up
with new things to nag about.

25:30.820 --> 25:31.905
You mean it?

25:36.284 --> 25:38.203
I guess I ruined our date.

25:38.286 --> 25:39.579
We can start over.

25:40.372 --> 25:42.207
Then we can do what you want now.

25:43.625 --> 25:45.043
All right. Let's go.

25:52.884 --> 25:54.594
Guide me to Hwiyeong-dong.

25:54.678 --> 25:56.680
GUIDE ME TO HWIYEONG-DONG

25:56.763 --> 25:59.933
Are we heading back?
Isn't there anything else you want to do?

26:00.016 --> 26:01.101
There is.

26:15.073 --> 26:18.493
- Is this what you wanted to do?
- Yes, I love this the most.

26:19.202 --> 26:22.122
Going to a cozy neighborhood pub
in the cold weather

26:22.205 --> 26:25.000
and chatting all night over some hot stew.

26:25.083 --> 26:27.252
Me too. I love this the most too.

26:30.171 --> 26:31.589
You two are ridiculous.

26:31.673 --> 26:34.426
If you're going to be here all night
with a single dish,

26:34.509 --> 26:37.679
at least give the owner a glance.

26:37.762 --> 26:41.182
Sol-i, this is kind of spicy.
Ung can't eat spicy food.

26:41.266 --> 26:42.892
Ung is fine.

26:42.976 --> 26:44.853
Ung can eat them now
since Yeon-su trained him.

26:44.936 --> 26:47.772
- Should we get something that isn't spicy?
- Well, then…

26:47.856 --> 26:49.316
Order whatever you want.

26:53.570 --> 26:55.780
This is the first time
my customers made me want to puke.

26:56.948 --> 26:59.117
You're doing a good job
holding it in, Sol-i.

26:59.200 --> 27:00.201
You can do it.

27:01.202 --> 27:03.330
Business isn't easy, you know.

27:03.413 --> 27:04.539
You can do it, Sol-i.

27:15.675 --> 27:17.177
- Do you want fish cakes?
- Yes.

27:17.260 --> 27:18.386
Here you go.

27:20.680 --> 27:22.390
- It's hot.
- It looks good.

27:22.474 --> 27:24.309
Let's try this.

27:29.606 --> 27:31.191
- Isn't it hot?
- Yes.

27:48.041 --> 27:50.960
You startled me, Grandma.

27:51.044 --> 27:52.879
What time did you come home last night?

27:54.047 --> 27:55.423
I'm not sure.

27:55.507 --> 27:56.716
You little brat!

28:00.470 --> 28:02.722
Were you with Ung last night?

28:03.598 --> 28:05.183
Well, yes.

28:05.266 --> 28:08.269
But I didn't get home that late, Grandma.

28:08.353 --> 28:11.398
Are you really going to go
to the finish line with him?

28:11.981 --> 28:16.361
Go where? I'm staying right here with you.

28:17.028 --> 28:18.780
Stop goofing around.

28:19.364 --> 28:22.283
If you really like Ung that much,

28:22.367 --> 28:24.077
bring him here.

28:24.160 --> 28:26.913
You'll make him uncomfortable.

28:26.996 --> 28:29.332
Last time, you totally bullied him.

28:29.416 --> 28:33.628
I have to hear what he thinks
about your relationship.

28:33.711 --> 28:35.964
Why are you so old-fashioned?

28:36.047 --> 28:38.174
You're getting way ahead of yourself.

28:38.258 --> 28:39.426
I'm taking a shower.

28:40.260 --> 28:44.472
Oh, and don't even think
about going to see Ung.

28:44.556 --> 28:47.225
I'll die of embarrassment if you do.

28:49.644 --> 28:52.147
That brat.
How can she talk to me like that?

28:54.274 --> 28:56.735
Right. You should head to work.
You'll be late.

28:56.818 --> 28:58.945
Don't ever make me drink
on a weekday again.

28:59.028 --> 29:02.699
Hey, you're the one who asked
to drink another bottle at the end.

29:02.782 --> 29:04.826
Don't even mention last night.

29:05.493 --> 29:08.788
- I should really get going now. Bye.
- Okay.

30:13.728 --> 30:15.939
I saw the interview you did.

30:16.523 --> 30:18.316
And the article that came out today.

30:18.399 --> 30:22.487
I felt I should thank you
for being so considerate.

30:22.570 --> 30:24.823
Thank you, NJ.

30:24.906 --> 30:27.283
He's drawing a line between us again.

30:56.187 --> 30:59.941
It took him days to text you,
and you're going to call him right away?

31:00.984 --> 31:02.777
I'm better than that.

31:03.319 --> 31:05.780
Let's just ignore it.

31:29.137 --> 31:30.263
Darn it.

31:57.165 --> 32:00.126
Dad, why did you order so much cabbage?

32:00.877 --> 32:02.629
Why do you think?

32:03.421 --> 32:06.090
It's kimchi season.

32:06.174 --> 32:09.636
Oh, right. I have a fever right now.

32:09.719 --> 32:12.180
- I should go home and rest.
- Oh, all right.

32:12.263 --> 32:13.598
Get some rest.

32:13.681 --> 32:15.183
And come back tomorrow.

32:15.266 --> 32:16.893
The cabbage arrives tomorrow.

32:16.976 --> 32:20.605
Jeez. Are you making kimchi
for the entire neighborhood?

32:20.688 --> 32:22.857
It's about time we stopped making so much.

32:22.941 --> 32:24.525
And sell some of your restaurants.

32:24.609 --> 32:27.570
If you keep going like this
you're bound to fail.

32:27.654 --> 32:31.616
What are you talking about?
Business is thriving right now.

32:31.699 --> 32:33.534
What will you do with all that money?

32:33.618 --> 32:35.036
Will you take it all with you?

32:35.119 --> 32:36.621
Like you told me to do,
I'll make a life for myself.

32:37.288 --> 32:39.123
Don't worry, Ung.

32:39.207 --> 32:42.794
I'll take every single cent with me.

32:44.253 --> 32:45.672
Mom, do you agree with him?

32:45.755 --> 32:48.132
Who do you think
should get the inheritance?

32:48.216 --> 32:51.928
Well, I doubt it'll go to you.

32:52.011 --> 32:56.349
What? I'm the only inheritor.
How can you not know?

32:56.432 --> 32:59.727
I think we can trust Yeon-su
to take care of our fortune though.

32:59.811 --> 33:04.065
Right. Yeon-su will do
a much better job than you.

33:04.148 --> 33:05.608
That's right.

33:05.692 --> 33:06.901
You're so harsh.

33:06.985 --> 33:08.861
You mean you like Yeon-su more than me?

33:08.945 --> 33:09.862
- Yes.
- Yes.

33:10.655 --> 33:11.531
But that's too bad.

33:13.408 --> 33:14.909
Yeon-su likes me.

33:17.453 --> 33:19.872
I can't believe what I just heard.

33:19.956 --> 33:22.542
I heard it too. That was close.

33:22.625 --> 33:25.336
I nearly puked on my son's face.

33:27.964 --> 33:30.967
Tell Yeon-su to come have dinner
when she gets off work.

33:31.050 --> 33:32.051
No, wait.

33:32.635 --> 33:34.387
She might feel pressured.

33:34.971 --> 33:37.473
Right. She'll feel pressured
if we keep asking her over.

33:37.557 --> 33:39.308
Should we pack her some side dishes?

33:39.392 --> 33:41.519
She can have them with her grandmother.

33:41.602 --> 33:43.604
No, we'll come together next time.

33:43.688 --> 33:45.773
Yeon-su said
she wanted to eat your braised fish.

33:45.857 --> 33:48.276
Really? Then tell me when you'll come.

33:48.359 --> 33:51.112
I'll make sure it's fresh and delicious.

33:51.195 --> 33:53.448
Should I go to the market tomorrow?

33:53.531 --> 33:54.866
No, wait.

33:54.949 --> 33:57.827
Should I bring her some side dishes?

34:04.375 --> 34:05.918
Did she leave the lights on again?

34:07.754 --> 34:10.214
LEEZAKAYA

34:14.093 --> 34:15.178
Sol-i?

34:15.928 --> 34:17.096
Are you here?

34:17.847 --> 34:19.390
Who is it? Eun-ho?

34:19.474 --> 34:21.225
Oh, you're here.

34:21.309 --> 34:22.810
You said you'd be closed today.

34:22.894 --> 34:26.481
Yes. I'm just here to organize some stuff.

34:26.564 --> 34:27.690
What brings you here?

34:27.774 --> 34:31.069
The lights were on
so I thought you forgot to turn them off.

34:31.152 --> 34:33.446
Don't treat me like
I'm a forgetful grandma.

34:33.529 --> 34:35.573
I don't forget things that often.

34:35.656 --> 34:38.159
I turned off the lights for you
five times this month.

34:38.951 --> 34:40.953
I appreciate that, but…

34:44.582 --> 34:47.085
You're so rude.

34:47.168 --> 34:49.253
How could you spit water
at the sight of me?

34:49.337 --> 34:52.924
Why are you dressed like that, Sol-i?

34:53.633 --> 34:55.593
No, repeat after me.

34:55.676 --> 34:58.971
"Sol-i, why do you look
prettier than usual today?"

35:00.014 --> 35:01.808
Are you going somewhere?

35:01.891 --> 35:03.935
What's going on? You're scaring me.

35:04.018 --> 35:07.688
I never thought my outfit
for the blind date would scare you.

35:07.772 --> 35:09.732
A blind date? Why?

35:13.236 --> 35:14.362
With who?

35:14.445 --> 35:16.864
I don't know much. My dad's setting me up.

35:17.490 --> 35:19.408
But he's handsome.

35:20.451 --> 35:21.619
So it's fine.

35:23.287 --> 35:26.457
If your dad's setting you up,
I guess he wants you to marry him.

35:26.999 --> 35:28.543
It's nothing that serious.

35:31.379 --> 35:34.215
It must be pretty awkward though.

35:34.799 --> 35:37.677
Why? I think it'll be really fun.

35:37.760 --> 35:40.263
Is it fun to eat with a stranger?

35:40.346 --> 35:43.057
I love meeting strangers. It's so fun.

35:43.141 --> 35:45.143
It'll be awkward.
You won't have much to talk about.

35:46.102 --> 35:49.438
Well, this actually suits me perfectly.

35:49.522 --> 35:52.233
I have such great conversations
with people I've just met.

35:52.859 --> 35:54.986
The conversation flows naturally.

36:01.117 --> 36:02.493
Your mouth again.

36:03.619 --> 36:06.455
Why are you pouting this time?

36:06.539 --> 36:10.042
You'll make me misunderstand you
if you keep acting like that.

36:10.126 --> 36:13.546
I used to write romance dramas.
Don't mess with me.

36:15.381 --> 36:17.341
What kind of misunderstanding?

36:17.425 --> 36:20.678
Oh, come on. Drop the act.

36:20.761 --> 36:23.139
I think I've told you about 35 times.

36:24.432 --> 36:25.725
I don't date younger guys.

36:34.525 --> 36:37.904
I know.
And this is my 35th time rejecting you.

36:43.618 --> 36:46.037
Have fun then.

36:47.997 --> 36:49.457
Okay.

36:51.918 --> 36:55.546
How old is that guy though?

36:56.297 --> 36:59.634
- He's much older than me.
- What's so good about an old guy?

37:03.721 --> 37:05.348
That rude brat.

37:10.228 --> 37:11.562
Yes?

37:13.189 --> 37:15.900
It's lunchtime.
Should we order something for you?

37:15.983 --> 37:17.693
It's fine. Eat without me.

37:18.486 --> 37:21.155
- But still…
- It's fine. Go.

37:21.989 --> 37:23.032
All right.

37:34.669 --> 37:36.629
You should at least have dinner.

37:36.712 --> 37:39.507
I don't want to eat.
Thanks for asking though.

37:40.299 --> 37:41.342
But still--

37:41.425 --> 37:43.803
I'll grab something later. Don't worry.

38:04.156 --> 38:05.992
I said I don't need to eat.

38:06.075 --> 38:08.869
You should still eat something, Mr. Kim.

38:16.585 --> 38:18.879
I came to see if you really are that busy

38:18.963 --> 38:21.549
or if you are just pretending to be busy.

38:22.133 --> 38:24.552
I didn't know you'd be skipping meals.

38:25.553 --> 38:27.638
- How did you get here?
- I took a cab.

38:28.264 --> 38:29.265
I mean…

38:29.348 --> 38:32.268
You should have answered my messages.

38:32.810 --> 38:34.603
Are you too busy? Should I wait outside?

38:35.187 --> 38:36.439
No, it's fine.

38:37.273 --> 38:39.108
Let's go have dinner then.

38:41.610 --> 38:42.486
Get up.

38:46.907 --> 38:48.659
Can you wait outside for a second?

38:49.660 --> 38:50.494
Okay.

39:02.423 --> 39:04.383
I wish our company had a cafeteria.

39:04.467 --> 39:05.843
Lucky you.

39:16.187 --> 39:17.688
This is good.

39:18.272 --> 39:21.192
Why aren't you eating all this
delicious food? It's such a waste.

39:21.275 --> 39:24.028
If it were me,
I'd be eating every single meal here.

39:29.909 --> 39:32.578
By the way, it looks like
you lost some weight.

39:33.120 --> 39:34.663
Haven't you been eating?

39:35.581 --> 39:38.584
Tae-hun told me you've been
practically living in the editing room.

39:39.919 --> 39:41.629
Well, I'm busy these days.

39:42.505 --> 39:45.091
I guess being a producer really is tough.

39:45.174 --> 39:48.219
Still, you should eat. We should
take care of our health at our age.

39:52.390 --> 39:54.141
But why did you come here?

39:55.226 --> 39:59.313
Oh, I wanted to ask if we could
check the footage beforehand.

39:59.397 --> 40:04.485
The footage about Soen and our project
should be checked with our client.

40:07.321 --> 40:10.908
- Okay, I'll send it to you.
- Can't I see it while I'm here?

40:11.409 --> 40:12.952
I'm a bit curious.

40:14.120 --> 40:16.372
I don't have much to show you.

40:16.455 --> 40:18.332
I heard the draft for episode one is out.

40:18.999 --> 40:20.709
I haven't made the revisions yet.

40:26.006 --> 40:28.384
- But Ji-ung.
- Yes?

40:29.009 --> 40:30.511
Why aren't you looking at me?

40:44.358 --> 40:46.152
Because I'm a mess right now.

40:47.528 --> 40:50.489
Why are you worried about that?

40:50.573 --> 40:52.032
Remember your birthday?

40:52.116 --> 40:54.910
I hung out with you
even when my eyes were all swollen.

40:55.744 --> 40:56.662
Don't forget that.

40:57.788 --> 40:58.956
Right.

41:05.296 --> 41:06.714
How have you been?

41:08.382 --> 41:11.177
I've been okay.

41:15.389 --> 41:16.307
Same as usual.

41:17.641 --> 41:19.768
And you? Have you been well?

41:20.936 --> 41:23.647
I've also been the same as usual.

41:35.868 --> 41:40.039
If I just ignore his message,
I'll seem even more pathetic.

41:40.122 --> 41:42.791
I should answer him casually

41:42.875 --> 41:44.418
to look like I don't care.

41:45.544 --> 41:46.378
Damn it.

41:47.630 --> 41:50.007
How deep did I bury this?

41:51.050 --> 41:53.594
Think before you do anything!

42:03.521 --> 42:06.440
Darn it. I give up.

42:12.363 --> 42:14.907
It's quite late already.

42:17.952 --> 42:19.995
It's still early though.

42:20.079 --> 42:22.289
It was so fun talking to you

42:22.373 --> 42:23.999
that I didn't notice the time.

42:25.042 --> 42:26.627
I never expected

42:26.710 --> 42:29.838
that I'd have such fun on a blind date.

42:29.922 --> 42:31.006
Right?

42:32.466 --> 42:36.303
If it's okay with you,
I'd like to talk with you a little more.

42:39.056 --> 42:40.516
I'd love that.

42:41.600 --> 42:42.851
Where should we go?

42:43.978 --> 42:46.605
- There's a place with clam stew--
- How about a cafe?

42:46.689 --> 42:49.066
That would be great.

42:50.067 --> 42:52.903
- Weren't you saying something though?
- No.

42:53.946 --> 42:55.614
Clam stew…

42:59.868 --> 43:01.203
The clams!

43:06.000 --> 43:08.669
Did I leave the door unlocked again?

43:09.253 --> 43:11.130
What's wrong with me?

43:12.047 --> 43:13.632
Where are my clams?

43:14.425 --> 43:15.843
Oh, my gosh!

43:15.926 --> 43:18.304
Jeez, you startled me.

43:18.887 --> 43:20.264
You gave me a fright.

43:20.347 --> 43:23.309
Hey, what are you doing here?

43:23.392 --> 43:26.270
See? You completely forgot.

43:26.812 --> 43:28.063
Did you bring them inside?

43:28.147 --> 43:32.026
I was going to ignore the package,
but I decided to be nice.

43:32.109 --> 43:33.819
You almost killed all the clams

43:33.902 --> 43:36.280
because you were preoccupied
with your date.

43:44.121 --> 43:45.956
Why did you come back so early?

43:46.040 --> 43:48.250
You were acting like
it was going to be so fun.

43:48.334 --> 43:50.169
It wasn't that fun, right?

43:50.794 --> 43:53.213
Isn't it awkward talking to someone
you've just met?

43:57.635 --> 43:59.345
You're right. It was boring.

44:01.639 --> 44:04.892
See? There's no way it'd be fun.

44:04.975 --> 44:05.976
It's obvious.

44:06.060 --> 44:09.021
Your conversations will keep
ending in silence.

44:09.104 --> 44:10.481
Yes, you're right.

44:10.564 --> 44:13.692
Sol-i, you should use that time
to get more customers.

44:13.776 --> 44:15.778
You need to pay back your loan.

44:18.238 --> 44:20.199
I told you it'd be boring.

44:22.493 --> 44:25.120
I had so much fun today.
Can I see you again next time?

44:26.705 --> 44:28.123
What is it?

44:29.333 --> 44:30.542
A spam message for a loan.

44:30.626 --> 44:34.254
I guess they have a knack
for finding people who need money.

44:34.338 --> 44:36.382
But do they send
spam messages at this hour?

44:37.007 --> 44:38.258
They're working hard.

44:43.639 --> 44:44.890
Do you want some clam stew?

44:47.726 --> 44:49.019
Sol-i!

44:49.103 --> 44:51.647
Hey, why are you shouting at me?

44:51.730 --> 44:54.400
Did you think you'd get to use
my labor for free?

44:55.067 --> 44:56.276
That's outrageous.

44:57.069 --> 45:00.364
I put some clams in the fridge.

45:01.824 --> 45:05.119
All right. I'll make you
an amazing clam stew.

45:07.538 --> 45:10.124
Let's empty the fridge
of all the soju tonight.

45:10.207 --> 45:12.960
Now you're starting to scare me.

45:13.794 --> 45:15.379
Why would we do that?

45:16.672 --> 45:18.549
Hello? Sol-i?

45:26.390 --> 45:28.183
I was just about to ring the bell.

45:28.267 --> 45:30.936
I wasn't just standing here,
so don't get the wrong idea.

45:31.019 --> 45:33.105
What are you doing here?

45:33.981 --> 45:36.692
I didn't say what I did
at the interview for you.

45:36.775 --> 45:38.360
I didn't mean anything by it.

45:39.027 --> 45:41.363
I'm not someone
who'd be so considerate of others.

45:42.573 --> 45:44.616
Did you come here to say that?

45:44.700 --> 45:46.118
You could have just texted me.

45:46.201 --> 45:47.661
My phone is…

45:48.495 --> 45:50.998
Anyway, it's not what you think. Okay?

45:51.707 --> 45:53.292
Go inside, then.

45:53.375 --> 45:54.793
I was on my way out.

45:54.877 --> 45:56.086
All right.

45:56.170 --> 45:57.463
Right.

46:00.757 --> 46:02.968
Oh, I guess I should leave.

46:03.719 --> 46:06.638
No, you came all the way here.
Let me give you some warm tea.

46:08.682 --> 46:09.892
No, wait.

46:10.642 --> 46:11.518
Well…

46:12.227 --> 46:14.897
Why don't I give you a ride…

46:15.481 --> 46:16.899
No, that's not it either.

46:19.776 --> 46:21.278
So I guess

46:22.029 --> 46:23.739
things are awkward between us now.

46:27.075 --> 46:29.661
I won't visit you randomly
like this anymore.

46:29.745 --> 46:31.538
Or keep texting or calling you.

46:31.622 --> 46:35.292
I wouldn't want to see my man
with another girl either.

46:35.375 --> 46:37.419
Especially if it's someone like me,

46:37.503 --> 46:39.379
it'd be quite stressful for her, right?

46:41.715 --> 46:43.217
About being friends…

46:43.717 --> 46:45.886
No, I'm not going to be friends with you.

46:45.969 --> 46:48.305
I don't make friends with men.

46:48.388 --> 46:50.098
I'm the one who's rejecting you.

46:50.682 --> 46:53.143
I'll get going, then.
You don't have to see me off.

46:58.524 --> 47:00.901
I didn't really like you that much.

47:00.984 --> 47:02.027
Just a little bit.

47:02.110 --> 47:05.072
In fact, I may have already
forgotten about it. That's how much.

47:06.990 --> 47:09.826
But I'm telling you just in case.

47:11.119 --> 47:12.788
Call me if you break up again.

47:29.680 --> 47:31.431
This is so cool.

47:32.099 --> 47:33.934
I've never seen stuff like this before.

47:36.228 --> 47:39.189
There's really not much to see.
I still have a lot to work on.

47:39.273 --> 47:40.774
It's fine, I understand.

47:40.857 --> 47:42.526
What should I press?

48:15.392 --> 48:17.060
PACKED MEALS

48:25.444 --> 48:28.071
Hello, my name is Choi Ung.

48:30.532 --> 48:31.783
My name is…

48:32.534 --> 48:35.120
Gosh, do we really have to do this?

48:35.621 --> 48:38.332
Ung was actually smirking back then.

48:38.415 --> 48:40.626
He's so sly.

48:42.586 --> 48:43.795
I'm sure it's obvious.

48:44.671 --> 48:47.716
- He liked me first.
- Honestly, I was a bit worried.

48:48.842 --> 48:50.844
- Maybe it's your camera work…
- Is that what she said?

48:50.927 --> 48:52.012
I look good in the video.

48:55.932 --> 48:57.184
Hey.

48:57.976 --> 48:59.227
When did you film this?

48:59.311 --> 49:01.021
I didn't even know you were filming.

49:03.023 --> 49:05.233
I'm impressed.

49:06.068 --> 49:07.903
You're a great producer, I give you that.

49:07.986 --> 49:09.655
You didn't miss a single moment.

49:15.327 --> 49:18.997
Was I really
looking at Ung with that expression?

49:36.640 --> 49:38.934
- Yeon-su. I'm sorry, but…
- Yes?

49:39.017 --> 49:42.437
- I should…
- Oh, right. You must be busy.

49:42.979 --> 49:45.941
Sorry. I took up too much of your time.

49:48.694 --> 49:50.570
Thanks. I enjoyed the video.

49:50.654 --> 49:53.949
I'll send you the file via email later.

49:54.700 --> 49:57.119
Okay. And take good care of your health.

49:58.620 --> 50:01.915
And let's have a meal together
with Ung next time.

50:03.291 --> 50:05.252
I don't think I'll have time anytime soon.

50:05.335 --> 50:07.003
Should we meet near your place?

50:07.087 --> 50:08.964
- At Ung's restaurant, or--
- I…

50:11.425 --> 50:12.843
I think I need some time.

50:13.593 --> 50:14.428
What?

50:16.304 --> 50:18.390
I need some time.

50:21.351 --> 50:24.396
All right. We can meet when you're free.

50:24.479 --> 50:25.939
I'll get going. Bye.

51:18.825 --> 51:22.162
Yeon-su said she'll be late today.

51:23.163 --> 51:25.248
Yes, I know.

51:26.666 --> 51:27.834
Then…

51:28.543 --> 51:31.546
you came when you knew I'd be here alone?

51:31.630 --> 51:33.632
- Yes.
- Really?

51:35.050 --> 51:38.303
You always used to just sit there
looking like a scared little puppy.

51:38.386 --> 51:39.721
What's the occasion?

51:42.015 --> 51:44.893
Well, did you have dinner?

51:44.976 --> 51:48.730
- I brought some side dishes.
- I ate.

51:49.523 --> 51:51.024
I see.

52:01.159 --> 52:03.161
- Don't get up.
- Okay.

52:03.245 --> 52:04.788
Let me get you some tea.

52:11.336 --> 52:12.629
Do you like jujube tea?

52:13.839 --> 52:15.423
I love it.

52:15.507 --> 52:17.759
I hate it because it smells rotten.

52:18.385 --> 52:20.470
Good. You can have what's left of it.

52:23.056 --> 52:26.226
- Let's go…
- Okay. Let's go.

52:26.309 --> 52:27.435
Let's go.

52:28.103 --> 52:29.187
Yeon-su!

52:29.771 --> 52:31.273
Did you just get off work?

52:31.356 --> 52:34.401
Yes, I'm heading home now.
Did you just close?

52:34.484 --> 52:36.903
Yes, we're about to head home too.

52:37.487 --> 52:39.865
- What about dinner?
- I just ate with Ji-ung.

52:39.948 --> 52:42.659
- Really?
- How is Ji-ung these days?

52:42.742 --> 52:44.244
We haven't seen him for a while.

52:44.327 --> 52:47.330
He seems pretty busy.
He's been stuck at the office.

52:48.039 --> 52:50.375
We should get some side dishes
for Ji-ung too.

52:50.458 --> 52:51.334
Right.

52:51.418 --> 52:54.713
Right. Ung just took
some side dishes for you.

52:55.422 --> 52:56.256
To where?

52:56.339 --> 52:59.217
To your house, of course.

53:00.176 --> 53:02.470
My grandma's home right now…

53:02.554 --> 53:05.390
Bring your grandma for a meal next time.

53:05.473 --> 53:07.851
I heard you wanted some braised fish.

53:07.934 --> 53:10.145
Yes. I will.

53:10.729 --> 53:12.230
You must be tired.

53:16.610 --> 53:19.029
You should hurry home and get some rest.

53:19.696 --> 53:21.823
All right. Bye, then.

53:21.907 --> 53:25.577
WITH UNG

53:27.746 --> 53:29.372
Go on.

53:43.428 --> 53:44.596
Where are you?

53:45.096 --> 53:46.806
I heard you came to my house.

53:46.890 --> 53:49.100
Yes. I'm back home now.

53:49.184 --> 53:51.645
Didn't you run into my grandmother?

53:51.728 --> 53:54.064
Did she say anything?
Did she scold you again?

53:54.147 --> 53:56.858
No, wait. I'll go to your house. Hang on.

53:58.944 --> 54:00.654
- I'll make you some tea.
- Okay.

54:02.113 --> 54:04.824
But why did you go to my house
when I wasn't there?

54:04.908 --> 54:06.993
Grandma must have given you an earful.

54:07.077 --> 54:08.161
She didn't.

54:12.707 --> 54:14.960
Do you read books like this these days?

54:16.753 --> 54:19.714
I haven't been reading much lately.

54:19.798 --> 54:21.174
I should read more too.

54:29.391 --> 54:31.059
ENSA ENROLLMENT FORM

54:32.060 --> 54:32.978
MUSEUM OF AVANT-GARDE
PARIS, FRANCE

54:33.061 --> 54:35.230
CONCERNING VARIABILITY AND INVARIABILITY›

54:35.313 --> 54:36.356
PROGRAMS, ALUMNI, ENROLLMENT

54:36.439 --> 54:37.691
What's this?

54:38.733 --> 54:39.693
It's nothing.

54:39.776 --> 54:43.321
It seems like a brochure
for an architecture school.

54:43.405 --> 54:45.448
Were you interested in architecture?

54:45.532 --> 54:48.618
Well, do you remember the architect
I told you I liked?

54:49.369 --> 54:51.871
He's a professor there,
so I was just looking at it.

54:51.955 --> 54:54.165
I see.

54:54.249 --> 54:57.836
You're always drawing buildings,
so of course you're interested.

54:58.336 --> 55:01.840
- I'm not.
- Why? It'll be nice to learn more.

55:01.923 --> 55:03.883
Why would I do that?

55:04.634 --> 55:06.720
It'll be such a bother.

55:06.803 --> 55:09.431
Drawing is exhausting as it is.

55:10.015 --> 55:10.932
You're right.

55:11.016 --> 55:13.893
Having one university diploma
is more than enough.

55:15.895 --> 55:18.023
- What?
- I didn't graduate.

55:19.441 --> 55:20.358
What?

55:21.401 --> 55:22.318
Why?

55:23.361 --> 55:25.363
I didn't really need to.

55:25.447 --> 55:28.199
Have you lost your mind?

55:28.283 --> 55:31.286
You attended school for years
and paid all that tuition.

55:31.369 --> 55:33.121
That all went to waste.

55:33.788 --> 55:37.584
You know I never really wanted
to attend university in the first place.

55:37.667 --> 55:39.085
I only attended because of you.

55:43.048 --> 55:44.841
Why are you so shocked?

55:44.924 --> 55:47.343
You knew I didn't like going to school.

55:49.429 --> 55:53.808
But still, how could you quit so easily?

55:54.893 --> 55:57.937
I didn't see the need for it personally.

55:59.397 --> 56:01.107
That's your reason?

56:01.191 --> 56:03.735
You can draw all the buildings you love

56:03.818 --> 56:05.987
and learn much more if you go there.

56:06.071 --> 56:08.573
Give this chance to someone
who needs it more than I do.

56:14.454 --> 56:17.373
Right. Eun-ho bought cookies. Hang on.

56:21.002 --> 56:24.881
By the way,
didn't Grandma say anything to you?

56:24.964 --> 56:28.093
If she said anything harsh,
don't take it personally.

56:28.176 --> 56:29.469
She always talks like that.

56:38.603 --> 56:41.648
Yeon-su. Can I ask you something?

56:42.941 --> 56:44.734
Yes. What is it?

56:47.153 --> 56:47.987
Back then…

56:53.868 --> 56:56.246
why did we break up?

57:14.139 --> 57:18.935
EPILOGUE

57:24.190 --> 57:26.109
I'm totally messed up.

57:30.238 --> 57:31.614
Drink this.

57:32.574 --> 57:33.741
Thanks.

57:35.869 --> 57:39.747
I saw you two
in the editing room a while ago.

57:39.831 --> 57:41.708
It reminded me of a movie.

57:41.791 --> 57:42.959
A movie?

57:43.042 --> 57:44.544
Love Actually.

57:45.170 --> 57:47.672
The part where the guy likes
his best friend's wife.

57:49.299 --> 57:50.633
Not Love and War?

57:52.010 --> 57:56.222
In the movie, he ends up confessing
his feelings on a sketchbook.

57:57.265 --> 57:59.392
And that became the most famous scene.

58:02.187 --> 58:03.730
What's going to be your ending?

58:06.065 --> 58:07.525
I'm not sure.

58:07.609 --> 58:09.319
I'm not in a movie.

58:11.905 --> 58:13.364
I'm in a documentary.

58:50.944 --> 58:52.403
That's what the media does.

58:52.487 --> 58:55.448
- It's Ung!
- It attracts unnecessary attention.

58:55.532 --> 58:56.533
Have you been well?

58:56.616 --> 58:58.952
By the way,
why don't you have any friends?

58:59.035 --> 59:01.913
Do you think we're in the same situation?

59:01.996 --> 59:04.874
Sol-i isn't yours anymore.

59:04.958 --> 59:07.126
What kind of person do I come off as?

59:07.710 --> 59:10.088
Do I look lost and aimless?

59:10.922 --> 59:12.590
That's what the past does to you.

59:13.591 --> 59:16.344
It causes you to make the same mistakes.

59:16.427 --> 59:20.056
You seemed so desperate to break up.

59:21.140 --> 59:26.145
Subtitle translation by: Ju-young Park
